# .trivyignore — accepted-risk waivers for container scans.
#
# Every entry carries an `exp:` expiry; when a waiver lapses, the finding
# becomes a gate failure again and must be re-evaluated (bump the carrying
# dependency, or renew with justification). Waivers apply to the publish-time
# Trivy gates (publish-circuit-images.yml) and the weekly audit
# (container-audit.yml). Each finding below was enumerated from a scan of the
# published digests on 2026-10-03; see docs/operations.md "Container
# hardening" for the full analysis.
#
# --- jackson inside freerouting.jar (circuit-tools AND circuit-server) -----
# freerouting-2.4.1.jar is a sha256-pinned upstream fat jar; 2.4.1 is the
# latest upstream release (2026-09-03) and carries jackson 2.22.1. No
# upstream release with patched jackson exists. Freerouting parses local
# project files and is not a network service. Re-evaluate at the next
# freerouting release bump.
CVE-2026-68497 exp:2027-01-03
CVE-2026-89407 exp:2027-01-03
CVE-2026-89425 exp:2027-01-03
CVE-2026-91776 exp:2027-01-03
CVE-2026-91777 exp:2027-01-03
#
# --- SDK-borne Python packages in /agent-server/.venv (circuit-server) -----
# The server image is assembled by the upstream OpenHands agent-server build
# (sdk:openhands-agent-server/1.53.0) on top of circuit-tools; these versions
# come from upstream's dependency resolution, not this repo's uv.lock (which
# already pins the fixed urllib3 2.8.0 / pypdf 6.19.0 / jaraco-context
# 6.1.2). pypdf, urllib3, virtualenv, wheel (via setuptools _vendor), and
# jaraco.context (via setuptools _vendor) findings clear on the next
# openhands-sdk bump — tracked in scripts/dependency_update_deferrals.json.
CVE-2026-102925 exp:2027-01-03
CVE-2026-102930 exp:2027-01-03
CVE-2026-102937 exp:2027-01-03
