#
# --- Dockerfiles embedded in the agent-server package (circuit-server) ----
# Trivy flags DS-0029 (apt-get without --no-install-recommends) on the
# Dockerfiles shipped as package resources under
# /agent-server/.venv/lib/python3.13/site-packages/openhands/agent_server/
# docker/ and /agent-server/openhands-agent-server/. They are upstream's
# nested-workspace build templates, not the recipe of the published image,
# and agent-server reads them at runtime when docker-workspace mode is
# requested, so they cannot be stripped. Our own Dockerfiles are covered by
# hadolint + `docker build --check`. Re-evaluate on the openhands-sdk bump —
# same deferral as the .venv findings.
DS-0029 exp:2027-01-03
#
# --- CIS baseline: build/CI tool images ---------------------------------
# DS-0002 (runs as root) and DS-0026 (no HEALTHCHECK): these images are CI
# build/tool containers, not deployed services. Non-root would change
# ownership of mounted workspace artifacts for no exploitable gain, and a
# HEALTHCHECK is meaningless for batch tooling (the publish and audit
# gates are the health checks). See docs/operations.md
# "Container hardening -> CIS baseline".
AVD-DS-0002 exp:2027-01-04
AVD-DS-0026 exp:2027-01-04
